WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.710
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.130
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.470
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.350
But, with you...

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.430
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.740
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.120
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Just to survive!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.660
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.500
Take this moment...

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.120
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.330
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.170
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.880
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.010
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.720
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.390
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.560
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.390
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.310
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:39.371
When determining whether the victim died by
hanging himself or by being strangled…

00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:42.841
If the victim had hung himself, the
mark will be angled like this.

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:48.880
On the other hand, if the victim had been strangled
to death, the mark will be horizontal like this.

00:01:49.281 --> 00:01:50.015
Who’s that?

00:01:50.715 --> 00:01:53.985
Hey, Kinta! Kinta!

00:01:54.519 --> 00:01:56.321
Rice! Another helping!

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.729
Just what I'd expect from the Class Q flunkies.

00:02:10.402 --> 00:02:11.469
Good work!

00:02:17.142 --> 00:02:19.844
So this is why you were sleeping during class?

00:02:20.145 --> 00:02:21.379
Ah, it's you guys!

00:02:23.748 --> 00:02:25.016
Here! We brought a snack.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:26.851
Oh, thank you!

00:02:27.852 --> 00:02:30.422
You saved me! I was starving!

00:02:31.956 --> 00:02:33.792
Aren’t you still in high school?

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:35.960
Why do you need a part-time job?

00:02:36.761 --> 00:02:39.798
Since I left home last year, I've been living by myself.

00:02:40.165 --> 00:02:42.100
Eh? You’re living by yourself?

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.302
Is your home far from here?

00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:45.770
Nah. It’s in the city.

00:02:46.271 --> 00:02:47.739
Huh? Then why?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.409
Could it be that your parents kicked you out?

00:02:52.644 --> 00:02:53.578
It’s not like that!

00:02:53.978 --> 00:02:57.649
It’s just that I don’t want to depend
on my parents too much.

00:03:03.321 --> 00:03:04.155
What was that?

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.257
Kinta!

00:03:07.225 --> 00:03:08.193
Sis!

00:03:09.227 --> 00:03:10.128
What happened?

00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:13.398
Oh, Sayaka-san! Call an ambulance!

00:03:13.598 --> 00:03:15.300
And call the police, too! Immediately!

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:16.501
Y-yes!

00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:24.008
What happened?

00:03:24.876 --> 00:03:25.643
Please come quickly!

00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:28.480
Sis! Sis!

00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:33.051
Sis!

00:03:33.184 --> 00:03:34.152
Sis!

00:03:57.409 --> 00:03:59.377
Okay. You guys can go now.

00:03:59.577 --> 00:04:00.111
Yes.

00:04:02.747 --> 00:04:04.883
The one who found the body, was you…

00:04:05.884 --> 00:04:09.354
…the victim’s younger sister, Shigeta Kumi-san?

00:04:09.854 --> 00:04:12.524
Yes. It was around 7:30.

00:04:13.057 --> 00:04:16.094
I work as a stage actress.

00:04:17.162 --> 00:04:20.465
When I returned home after work, my sister was…

00:04:26.171 --> 00:04:26.771
Sis?

00:04:30.208 --> 00:04:31.109
Are you there?

00:04:33.878 --> 00:04:34.512
Sis?

00:04:37.615 --> 00:04:40.185
And you called the police immediately after that?

00:04:41.152 --> 00:04:43.087
She was the one who made the call.

00:04:45.223 --> 00:04:47.325
You’re Kinoshita Sayaka, the housekeeper?

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:48.726
Y-yes.

00:04:49.627 --> 00:04:57.535
Until Kumi-san returned, you and the victim,
Akemi-san, were the only ones in the house, right?

00:04:59.037 --> 00:04:59.771
Am I wrong?

00:05:00.305 --> 00:05:02.273
No. That’s correct. Yes.

00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:06.711
Hey, what are you guys doing?

00:05:07.178 --> 00:05:07.679
Huh?

00:05:09.581 --> 00:05:12.550
The mark on the victim’s neck was horizontal.

00:05:12.817 --> 00:05:16.888
And also, the nail marks indicate some sort of
struggle; It must have been strangulation.

00:05:17.155 --> 00:05:19.023
What are you kids still doing here?

00:05:19.591 --> 00:05:20.391
Get up and go home!

00:05:24.429 --> 00:05:25.997
D-DDS!

00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:28.166
The detective academy?

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.367
Y-yes…

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.605
Please excuse my rudeness!

00:05:35.273 --> 00:05:36.307
Ah, sir!

00:05:36.608 --> 00:05:38.343
They’re from DDS.

00:05:39.177 --> 00:05:40.278
DDS, eh?

00:05:40.945 --> 00:05:42.780
Please feel free to investigate.

00:05:42.981 --> 00:05:43.515
Yes.

00:05:44.382 --> 00:05:47.485
Please tell me one thing. What
was the murder weapon?

00:05:47.986 --> 00:05:52.457
It seems to have been a thin string of some
sort, but we haven’t found it yet.

00:05:53.992 --> 00:05:54.659
Well, then…

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.430
Thanks for your time. We’ll continue
with the investigation.

00:05:59.898 --> 00:06:02.767
Hey, hey. That notepad had quite an impact!

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:07.272
So It was true that this notepad has
as much impact as a police badge.

00:06:07.405 --> 00:06:09.407
But what’s even cooler is this…

00:06:10.375 --> 00:06:14.646
A fingerprint detection set, a special all-purpose
knife, lock-picking tools…

00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:17.115
…and even a table of random sampling
numbers for decoding!

00:06:17.482 --> 00:06:20.051
Okay! Let’s try detecting fingerprints first!

00:06:20.552 --> 00:06:21.052
Yeah.

00:06:22.954 --> 00:06:24.322
Let’s begin over there.

00:06:25.823 --> 00:06:28.793
Umm… How do you use it?

00:06:29.527 --> 00:06:30.995
You sprinkle out the powder.

00:06:31.429 --> 00:06:31.896
Oh, yeah.

00:06:33.131 --> 00:06:35.500
The main ingredient in the powder
is crushed aluminum.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.436
If there are any fingerprints, the grease
from the prints will show up.

00:06:39.203 --> 00:06:42.040
Umm… We already checked there.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.508
Oh, is that so?

00:06:43.975 --> 00:06:45.376
Then were any fingerprints detected?

00:06:46.077 --> 00:06:49.247
Yes, they were. But they were all from the victim.

00:06:54.452 --> 00:06:56.487
I bet they haven’t checked here!

00:06:59.991 --> 00:07:02.160
You know, there’s no point in checking there.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.628
It can’t hurt to try.

00:07:07.465 --> 00:07:07.966
They showed up!

00:07:10.001 --> 00:07:10.535
Watch out!

00:07:14.839 --> 00:07:15.607
I-I'm sorry!

00:07:16.307 --> 00:07:17.642
No, it was my fault.

00:07:18.343 --> 00:07:20.111
What’s all the fuss about, Sayaka-san?

00:07:20.778 --> 00:07:21.713
I'm sorry!

00:07:21.913 --> 00:07:23.081
It was my fault.

00:07:24.515 --> 00:07:25.416
Please be careful.

00:07:29.053 --> 00:07:29.821
Don’t worry.

00:07:30.288 --> 00:07:31.489
Ah, okay.

00:07:38.229 --> 00:07:38.930
Pardon me.

00:07:40.565 --> 00:07:41.265
What’s that?

00:07:41.666 --> 00:07:44.469
It’s the same thing that was on the victim’s leg.

00:07:48.339 --> 00:07:49.440
Let’s investigate it later.

00:07:54.946 --> 00:07:56.280
They’re the victim’s.

00:07:56.781 --> 00:07:57.682
Too bad.

00:07:57.882 --> 00:07:58.816
You don’t have to say that!

00:08:00.585 --> 00:08:03.254
But, why are they in such a high place?

00:08:07.692 --> 00:08:10.461
The presumed time of death
was approximately 4 p.m.

00:08:11.229 --> 00:08:14.766
Just before she was murdered, the victim sent a fax.

00:08:21.673 --> 00:08:23.875
The victim was a lyricist.

00:08:24.809 --> 00:08:27.211
Did you hear any noise around that time?

00:08:28.579 --> 00:08:30.014
No. Nothing.

00:08:30.848 --> 00:08:33.551
And also, at the time of the crime…

00:08:33.551 --> 00:08:37.722
…it seems that there was a neighborhood
wives meeting next door, but…

00:08:38.623 --> 00:08:41.492
Nobody saw anyone suspicious.

00:08:41.926 --> 00:08:43.695
Why didn’t you notice anything?

00:08:44.228 --> 00:08:47.865
If you had noticed something,
my sister might not have died.

00:08:48.599 --> 00:08:49.901
Normally, you’d notice something!

00:08:50.168 --> 00:08:52.570
You two were in the same building, weren’t you?

00:08:52.804 --> 00:08:53.604
Y-yes…

00:08:54.706 --> 00:08:56.307
By the way, Kumi-san.

00:08:57.675 --> 00:09:03.514
I heard you and your sister were having a
quarrel about your uncles inheritance.

00:09:06.084 --> 00:09:07.151
Who told you that?

00:09:11.789 --> 00:09:13.558
Is that true, Kumi-san?

00:09:15.059 --> 00:09:15.927
It’s true.

00:09:16.394 --> 00:09:18.796
But it wasn’t that big a deal.

00:09:19.397 --> 00:09:24.635
Oh, by the way, I remember my sister said
something recently that has me a little worried.

00:09:25.503 --> 00:09:26.337
What was it?

00:09:26.771 --> 00:09:30.408
She told me that money had been disappearing
from her wallet recently.

00:09:30.975 --> 00:09:31.809
Do you know about it?

00:09:32.176 --> 00:09:33.778
No. Not really.

00:09:34.078 --> 00:09:36.114
Oh, my. Feigning ignorance.

00:09:36.781 --> 00:09:39.484
It was you, wasn’t it? You did it, didn’t you?

00:09:39.584 --> 00:09:41.152
No, you’re mistaken!

00:09:41.786 --> 00:09:43.121
Tell the truth!

00:09:43.888 --> 00:09:45.656
Now, now. Please calm down!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:46.891
Let go of me!

00:09:48.392 --> 00:09:49.594
By the way, Kinoshita-san.

00:09:50.027 --> 00:09:53.865
It was three and a half hours before
Kumi-san came back home.

00:09:54.332 --> 00:09:56.567
You didn’t go and check on Akemi-san
even once during that time?

00:09:57.101 --> 00:10:00.538
Akemi-Sensei had always told me not to go
into her room while she was working.

00:10:01.139 --> 00:10:02.740
She didn’t want anybody to disturb her work.

00:10:03.241 --> 00:10:06.210
She even told me never to knock
or to transfer phone calls.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.681
I-I'm telling the truth.

00:10:11.649 --> 00:10:13.584
You’re the one who killed my sister, aren’t you?

00:10:14.051 --> 00:10:15.052
No!

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:16.587
You murderer!

00:10:17.388 --> 00:10:19.157
She’s not a murderer!

00:10:19.524 --> 00:10:20.358
Kinta.

00:10:20.958 --> 00:10:22.059
What makes you say that?

00:10:22.693 --> 00:10:23.461
Her eyes!

00:10:24.796 --> 00:10:26.264
They aren’t the eyes of a person who is lying!

00:10:29.133 --> 00:10:35.439
Oh, I see! Students at DDS learn how to tell if
someone is lying by the reaction of their pupils.

00:10:36.374 --> 00:10:37.909
There’s no skill like that.

00:10:38.509 --> 00:10:40.378
Eh? Then what…?

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.583
I sensed it! With my mind’s eye!

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.018
Huh?

00:10:49.053 --> 00:10:52.256
Kumi-san, aren’t you the murderer?

00:10:52.957 --> 00:10:55.960
With the issue of your uncle’s inheritance,
you had a motive.

00:10:58.462 --> 00:11:01.232
But I have an alibi.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:07.705
I was acting on the stage of the new theater
that just opened in Shimokitayama.

00:11:09.207 --> 00:11:13.277
At 4 p.m. when the crime was committed,
I was in the middle of the show.

00:11:15.179 --> 00:11:18.816
The 1000 people in the audience are my witnesses.

00:11:27.526 --> 00:11:29.595
She’s definitely the murderer!

00:11:30.162 --> 00:11:31.263
But it’s perfect…

00:11:31.964 --> 00:11:33.599
She has a perfect alibi.

00:11:35.734 --> 00:11:40.172
The hell with that alibi! I'll crush that alibi!

00:11:40.706 --> 00:11:41.573
But how?

00:11:42.274 --> 00:11:45.043
If you’re that sure, Kinta, I'll tag along!

00:12:03.295 --> 00:12:03.896
Yes?

00:12:06.665 --> 00:12:08.500
I do have a car, but…

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.415
Awesome car!

00:12:23.615 --> 00:12:25.551
Hey, isn’t that a Rolls Royce?

00:12:25.984 --> 00:12:27.453
I wonder what kind of person owns that.

00:12:28.086 --> 00:12:30.456
By the way, Kazuma sure is late!

00:12:32.491 --> 00:12:34.927
What are you guys doing? I'm right here!

00:12:36.528 --> 00:12:37.896
K-Kazuma!

00:12:39.565 --> 00:12:40.732
Excuse me…

00:12:41.166 --> 00:12:43.902
You were this rich?

00:12:44.269 --> 00:12:46.872
And what are we doing?

00:12:49.608 --> 00:12:52.544
The performance began at
2 pm. and ended at 6 pm.

00:12:52.945 --> 00:12:57.349
There was a 30-minute intermission
from 3:30 to 4:00.

00:12:57.883 --> 00:13:03.055
We’re checking if she could have committed
the crime during that intermission.

00:13:03.822 --> 00:13:04.690
Well, let’s go!

00:13:04.857 --> 00:13:05.157
Right.

00:13:07.092 --> 00:13:07.526
Start!

00:13:10.863 --> 00:13:12.431
See you later, Kinta!

00:13:40.792 --> 00:13:41.560
What’s this?

00:13:41.793 --> 00:13:43.562
It’s a homard sandwich.

00:13:44.296 --> 00:13:45.564
You’ve never had one before?

00:13:45.998 --> 00:13:47.866
Eh? Let’s see…

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.134
It’s delicious!

00:13:49.735 --> 00:13:51.803
Please look at this, you two.

00:13:52.404 --> 00:13:55.207
I this is what I got when I searched
the Internet for Shigeta Kumi.

00:13:55.941 --> 00:13:57.476
An online bulletin board, eh?

00:13:59.111 --> 00:14:01.380
What is this? “I'll kill you.“?

00:14:02.247 --> 00:14:03.982
They’re all nasty messages to Kumi-san!

00:14:05.083 --> 00:14:10.155
It seems that all these were sent to
Kumi-san by the same person.

00:14:10.756 --> 00:14:15.093
Eh!? Isn't this an anonymous bulletin
board? How do you know that?

00:14:15.694 --> 00:14:18.864
Look carefully at the times they
were sent and at the contents.

00:14:19.631 --> 00:14:24.803
For example, from number 151 to number 156…

00:14:25.904 --> 00:14:28.874
All together, there are 6 mails that
are addressed to Kumi-san.

00:14:29.508 --> 00:14:31.610
And they were all sent at one minute intervals.

00:14:32.711 --> 00:14:36.682
I see now. The same person
is writing it continuously.

00:14:37.549 --> 00:14:40.018
Whoa! Kinta’s fast!

00:14:49.294 --> 00:14:50.162
What was your time?

00:14:51.229 --> 00:14:52.364
29 minutes.

00:14:53.665 --> 00:14:55.033
We had 31 minutes.

00:14:55.567 --> 00:14:57.736
Alright! The alibi has been crushed!

00:14:58.403 --> 00:15:00.205
The intermission was 30 minutes!

00:15:01.473 --> 00:15:04.209
You do realize that you’d have to make & round trip?

00:15:04.476 --> 00:15:06.411
O-Oh, that’s right…

00:15:06.912 --> 00:15:10.882
It would be impossible unless she
used a helicopter or something.

00:15:11.383 --> 00:15:13.352
That’s right! She used a helicopter!

00:15:13.719 --> 00:15:14.820
No. No.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:19.024
Normally, this would be a perfect setting
to use a stand-in trick, but…

00:15:19.291 --> 00:15:20.692
That must be it!

00:15:20.959 --> 00:15:24.296
She was playing the leading role. It’s impossible.

00:15:28.634 --> 00:15:31.003
But I'm somehow not convinced yet…

00:15:32.237 --> 00:15:34.506
Let’s go check out the crime scene again!

00:15:40.912 --> 00:15:43.649
Okay. Firstly, the condition of the corpse.

00:15:44.316 --> 00:15:47.986
The victim, Akemi-san, was
strangled to death, right?

00:15:48.553 --> 00:15:51.390
Yeah. It was clearly strangulation.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.825
There were even nail marks from the struggle.

00:15:54.159 --> 00:15:57.362
But why was she curled up like that?

00:16:00.699 --> 00:16:01.333
Huh?

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.935
Your body bent the other way.

00:16:04.302 --> 00:16:05.504
Was there anything else?

00:16:06.938 --> 00:16:09.875
A sprig like this was found near the body.

00:16:10.776 --> 00:16:13.011
I researched it, and found out
that it’s called Stone Willow.

00:16:14.246 --> 00:16:17.282
The corpse’s unnatural posture… The Stone Willow…

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.785
How are those two related?

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.825
But even if we knew that, I doubt
that it would overturn her alibi.

00:16:27.459 --> 00:16:28.694
That will be hard.

00:16:29.561 --> 00:16:32.998
Damn it! Anything! Isn't there anything else?

00:16:33.465 --> 00:16:36.902
Aren’t there any dues that will break
Shigeta Kumi’s impregnable alibi?

00:16:38.637 --> 00:16:39.805
What are you doing?

00:16:40.272 --> 00:16:41.973
I'm looking for clues!

00:16:42.908 --> 00:16:43.842
Crap!

00:16:49.047 --> 00:16:49.815
This is…

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.853
The reason why the victim’s fingerprints were here…

00:16:57.589 --> 00:16:58.390
That’s it!

00:16:59.858 --> 00:17:01.626
Kinta! Are you all right?

00:17:03.762 --> 00:17:04.796
I got it!

00:17:07.632 --> 00:17:10.869
What do you want? I have a performance at 8 pm.

00:17:11.503 --> 00:17:12.804
This won’t take much time.

00:17:13.338 --> 00:17:16.708
But you said you knew who the culprit is…

00:17:17.075 --> 00:17:19.778
It’s already obvious who it is.

00:17:20.145 --> 00:17:20.979
The murderer is…

00:17:21.046 --> 00:17:22.247
It’s not Sayaka-san.

00:17:24.149 --> 00:17:25.684
There’s no way Sayaka-san could have done it.

00:17:28.019 --> 00:17:31.089
What are you trying to say? Who else is there?

00:17:31.623 --> 00:17:32.758
There are three hints.

00:17:33.391 --> 00:17:36.962
The corpse’s unnatural posture and the fingerprints
detected above the window.

00:17:37.696 --> 00:17:40.031
And also the sprig that was on the corpse.

00:17:40.766 --> 00:17:44.669
Shigeta Kumi-san, the murderer is you after all!

00:17:52.377 --> 00:17:54.012
What is this guy talking about?

00:17:54.412 --> 00:17:56.481
I have an alibi.

00:17:56.848 --> 00:18:02.687
Yeah. You do have an alibi that proves
that you were at the theater, but…

00:18:03.288 --> 00:18:09.394
In this case, the problem isn’t the culprit’s alibi.
The real problem is the victim’s alibi.

00:18:10.929 --> 00:18:12.564
The victim’s alibi, you say?

00:18:12.931 --> 00:18:14.566
Akemi-san’s alibi?

00:18:15.033 --> 00:18:16.968
She was in the house the whole time.

00:18:17.602 --> 00:18:19.437
Who can prove that?

00:18:20.105 --> 00:18:21.673
Even Sayaka-san didn’t see her.

00:18:24.876 --> 00:18:30.048
The fax that my sister sent before she died
is the evidence that she was here.

00:18:33.685 --> 00:18:39.124
I just sent a fax using the victim’s computer;
the computer can do that automatically.

00:18:39.758 --> 00:18:46.531
By placing the copy in advance, she
created an alibi that she was here.

00:18:47.632 --> 00:18:50.635
It would seem like she sent the fax herself.

00:18:51.603 --> 00:18:54.239
An alibi? For what?

00:18:54.773 --> 00:18:57.209
In order to go and meet you at the theater!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:06.718
The victim had to leave the house without
being noticed by Sayaka-san.

00:19:07.352 --> 00:19:09.688
That’s why she left through this window.

00:19:13.792 --> 00:19:17.462
That was when the victim’s fingerprints
were left on the window frame.

00:19:20.498 --> 00:19:22.634
Why would my sister do that?

00:19:23.702 --> 00:19:27.606
To kill you in order to get the full amount
of your uncle’s inheritance.

00:19:29.875 --> 00:19:30.876
Please take a look at this.

00:19:31.443 --> 00:19:32.544
What is this?

00:19:33.011 --> 00:19:37.649
These are messages and even death
threats sent to Kumi-san.

00:19:38.783 --> 00:19:43.355
With help from this bulletin board’s
owner and the domain provider…

00:19:43.922 --> 00:19:49.127
We know they were sent from the computer
in this room, in other words, by Akemi-san.

00:19:49.828 --> 00:19:51.930
After deciding to murder Kumi-san at the theater…

00:19:52.197 --> 00:19:55.100
…she was probably trying to make it look
like there was a stalker of some sort.

00:19:56.835 --> 00:20:00.038
It seems that Akemi-san didn’t know
that it’s possible to determine…

00:20:00.038 --> 00:20:05.043
…who sent the messages using the computer’s IP
address even if they were made anonymously.

00:20:06.311 --> 00:20:09.014
You were probably surprised too.

00:20:09.981 --> 00:20:14.719
Akemi-san tried to kill you while you were on break.

00:20:15.453 --> 00:20:18.423
But then, the opposite happened,
and you killed Akemi-san.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:23.962
After your break, you hid Akemi-san’s body in the
dressing room and continued acting in the show.

00:20:24.562 --> 00:20:28.199
And then, after the show was over,
you brought her body back home.

00:20:32.328 --> 00:20:32.995
Sis?

00:20:36.465 --> 00:20:37.333
Are you there?

00:20:39.969 --> 00:20:40.636
Sis?

00:20:42.371 --> 00:20:44.440
You screamed even though nobody was there.

00:20:46.942 --> 00:20:47.843
Sis!

00:20:49.178 --> 00:20:50.012
What happened?

00:20:50.012 --> 00:20:51.447
And Sayaka-san came running up.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.349
Oh, Sayaka-san! Call the ambulance!

00:20:53.716 --> 00:20:55.484
And call the police, too! Immediately!

00:20:56.251 --> 00:20:56.685
Y-Yes!

00:20:59.922 --> 00:21:02.157
During the time after you sent her away…

00:21:04.426 --> 00:21:09.598
The reason why Akemi-san was curled up is because
she was kept in the suitcase the whole time!

00:21:12.201 --> 00:21:14.103
Sis! Sis!

00:21:17.706 --> 00:21:19.842
Sis! Sis!

00:21:24.279 --> 00:21:26.515
You sure were a good actor.

00:21:27.483 --> 00:21:28.484
It wasn’t me!

00:21:29.118 --> 00:21:30.419
There’s nobody else besides you!

00:21:31.487 --> 00:21:36.625
You used the victim’s alibi in order
to create your own alibi!

00:21:37.326 --> 00:21:39.194
That can’t be! Do you have any evidence?

00:21:39.795 --> 00:21:41.430
I'll sue you for slander!

00:21:41.864 --> 00:21:43.132
We have evidence.

00:21:43.999 --> 00:21:46.135
The sprig that was stack on Akemî-san.

00:21:47.002 --> 00:21:48.170
It was a sprig of Stone Willow.

00:21:49.471 --> 00:21:52.941
From the one that was given to you
and was in your dressing room.

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:54.410
Is that true?

00:21:55.344 --> 00:21:57.613
I don’t know! I don’t know!

00:21:58.013 --> 00:22:02.484
Somebody! Somebody did it
to place the blame on me!

00:22:03.052 --> 00:22:04.386
Are you still going to play innocent?

00:22:05.187 --> 00:22:06.622
If you want, we can check again.

00:22:07.589 --> 00:22:11.326
We can check if there are fingerprints from
the victim in a theater that just opened!

00:22:29.445 --> 00:22:31.780
Thank you for believing me.

00:22:32.214 --> 00:22:36.285
Um, you know… It’s a detective’s job
to look into this kind of thing…

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:38.620
Kinta!

00:22:39.054 --> 00:22:39.922
Are you all right!?

00:22:40.456 --> 00:22:41.757
How embarrassing…

00:22:44.726 --> 00:22:49.098
Is that so? You guys found the answer by
looking at the case from another angle.

00:22:49.631 --> 00:22:51.200
Reverse thinking, eh?

00:22:51.567 --> 00:22:54.803
Detectives must not look at a case
from a single perspective.

00:22:55.104 --> 00:22:58.006
They must look from multiple perspectives.

00:22:58.907 --> 00:22:59.575
Great job!

00:23:00.576 --> 00:23:02.010
Keep up your efforts from now on.

00:23:02.377 --> 00:23:02.845
Yes!

00:23:04.046 --> 00:23:07.883
By the way, this DDS notepad had quite an impact!

00:23:08.383 --> 00:23:11.553
The police were very cooperative after they saw it.

00:23:12.354 --> 00:23:15.824
Well, it is made so that your investigations
will go smoothly, but…

00:23:16.625 --> 00:23:20.529
I don’t want you guys to rely
on its influence too much.

00:23:21.029 --> 00:23:22.631
Yes! We understand!

00:23:23.665 --> 00:23:27.236
But couldn’t you get on the train for free with this?

00:23:27.803 --> 00:23:30.672
It’s kind of hard getting here when I don’t get paid.

00:23:32.407 --> 00:23:33.475
Hey, hey.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:47.530
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:24:02.090
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:09.180
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:14.810
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:21.020
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:21.150 --> 00:24:26.570
I will see you off.

00:24:26.820 --> 00:24:36.410
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.673 --> 00:24:39.275
A young art genius is murdered.

00:24:39.942 --> 00:24:42.011
Suspicious people seek the dead artist’s paintings.

00:24:42.712 --> 00:24:45.414
The hidden truth that is in the scattered
puzzle at the crime scene.

00:24:46.315 --> 00:24:49.952
The victim’s last bit of energy becomes
the key to solving the mystery.

00:24:51.053 --> 00:24:52.522
Words aren’t the only message.

00:24:53.295 --> 00:24:54.296
There's only one answer!

00:24:56.626 --> 00:24:58.161
Why doesn’t this open?

00:24:58.528 --> 00:25:01.497
We’ll be late for class!
Damn it. Alright, take this!

00:25:03.466 --> 00:25:04.367
What are you doing?

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:05.601
Is this a trick door?

00:25:06.102 --> 00:25:09.972
Ah, no, I put knobs on the doors because
they look bad without them.

00:25:10.373 --> 00:25:10.973
Huh?
